_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Mock running-state flips even when start/stop fails**

Line 46 and Line 55 update `isRunning` unconditionally. In failure-path tests, this can mask service-state bugs by putting the mock in an impossible state.



<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
   `@override`
   Future<ServiceRequestResult> startService({
     required int serviceId,
     List<ForegroundServiceTypes>? serviceTypes,
@@
   }) async {
     calls.add('startService');
-    isRunning = true;
+    if (startResult is ServiceRequestSuccess) {
+      isRunning = true;
+    }
     lastServiceTypes = serviceTypes;
     lastNotificationIcon = notificationIcon;
     return startResult;
   }

   `@override`
   Future<ServiceRequestResult> stopService() async {
     calls.add('stopService');
-    isRunning = false;
+    if (stopResult is ServiceRequestSuccess) {
+      isRunning = false;
+    }
     return stopResult;
   }
```
</details>

